From: A7om <hatter6822@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw/display/bcm2835_fb: Answer requests on the framebuffer
 channel again

A request on the mailbox's framebuffer channel raises the mailbox's
interrupt line from bcm2835_fb's write handler, and bcm2835_mbox reads
the response from bcm2835_fb's registers there and then. Since the
memory API blocks re-entrant I/O, that read fails: the mailbox takes a
0 for the response, and as bcm2835_fb, never read, keeps its line up and
the channel busy, it takes another and another until its queue to the
ARM is full. The guest reads a 0 where it expects the channel number,
the channel takes no further request, and the responses of every other
channel queue up behind the zeros.

Mark the registers as re-entrancy safe, as bcm2835_property's were when
the guard came in.

Fixes: a2e1753b8054 ("memory: prevent dma-reentracy issues")
---
 hw/display/bcm2835_fb.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/bcm2835_fb.c b/hw/display/bcm2835_fb.c
index bd58f625..7e88f942 100644
--- a/hw/display/bcm2835_fb.c
+++ b/hw/display/bcm2835_fb.c
@@ -386,6 +386,14 @@ static void bcm2835_fb_init(Object *obj)
 
     memory_region_init_io(&s->iomem, obj, &bcm2835_fb_ops, s, TYPE_BCM2835_FB,
                           0x10);
+
+    /*
+     * Like bcm2835_property's, a request raises the mailbox's interrupt
+     * line, on which bcm2835_mbox reads the response from iomem while the
+     * write is still in progress: mark iomem as re-entrancy safe.
+     */
+    s->iomem.disable_reentrancy_guard = true;
+
     sysbus_init_mmio(SYS_BUS_DEVICE(s), &s->iomem);
     sysbus_init_irq(SYS_BUS_DEVICE(s), &s->mbox_irq);
 }
